# SYNTHESISED to exercise the swimlane timeline's lane packing and stall
# detection. Two RPC spans -- one aws, one google -- genuinely overlap in
# time, which is what gives the log a peak concurrency of 2 for the stall
# annotation to measure its windows against; per-provider lane packing draws
# them on separate rows whether they overlap or not. A third aws span then
# runs alone for 5s after both earlier spans have finished, giving the stall
# annotation a real solo window to find. The line shape is
# testdata/two-providers.log's "Received downstream response" verbatim. The
# first line is not itself a response: it exists only to anchor the
# scanner's base clock a few seconds before the first real span, so that
# span's start is not clamped to zero by ReportedBuilder (see the doc
# comment on span.Span). Values are invented; no line here is from a real
# run.
